        "problem": "Let $u=3i-2k$ and $v=-2i+j+5k.$ Determine $u\\times v.$",
        "worked_solution": "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot 1)i-(3\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot (-2))j+(3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =(0+2)i-(15-4)j+(3-0)k \\\\  & =2i-11j+3k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
